IMPORT prelude

-- Arms Offences Act 1973 (Singapore) -- the definitions in s 2, the gun offences and their punishments (ss 3 to 8), the
-- occupier's presumption of possession (s 9), and the Schedule of scheduled offences.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/7/2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/AOA1973.txt, with amendments to Act 3 of 2021 (in force 1 July 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The Act is short, so almost all of it
-- is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 11 (saving of other written law), s 12 (Minister's power to amend the
-- Schedule), the Kidnapping Act 1961 and Vandalism Act 1966 items of the Schedule beyond a flag, Penal Code s 458A (not
-- an integer section number), the content of the Penal Code Chapter 4 exceptions and of the Guns, Explosives and
-- Weapons Control Act 2021, to which "gun", "unlawful possession" and "trafficking in guns" all point.
--
-- NOTE ON THE DEPOSIT. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body by one line
-- (it lists "3A. Unlawful possession of gun with criminal intent", which is s 3 in the body). This encoding follows the
-- BODY's numbering.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Arms Offences Act 1973 -- guns`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `lo` IS A NUMBER, `hi` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lies between` IF
    `n` >= `lo` AND `n` <= `hi`

§§ `2 -- definitions`

-- "imitation gun" means an object that, "regardless of its colour, weight or composition or the presence or absence of any
-- moveable part, substantially duplicates in appearance a gun but that is not a gun, or any such object that is produced
-- and identified as a toy". "gun" has the meaning in s 3 of the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021 "and
-- excludes an imitation gun".
DECLARE Object IS ONE OF
    `a real gun`
    `a replica that looks like a gun`
    `a toy that looks like a gun`
    `a brightly coloured plastic replica that looks like a gun`
    `an object that does not look like a gun`

GIVEN `the object` IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is an imitation gun` IF
    CONSIDER `the object`
    WHEN `a replica that looks like a gun` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a toy that looks like a gun` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a brightly coloured plastic replica that looks like a gun` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "unlawful possession", in relation to a gun, means possession of a gun when -- (a) "not authorised by a licence or a
-- class licence" under the 2021 Act; (b) "not in accordance with the conditions of a licence or a class licence mentioned
-- in paragraph (a); AND" (c) "not exempt from" the 2021 Act. The three limbs are joined by AND. Read literally, a licensee
-- who breaches the licence's conditions is still "authorised by a licence", so limb (a) is not met and the possession is
-- not "unlawful possession". The encoding follows that literal reading. That this is a literal reading, and may not be
-- what was meant, is an inference; the text does not say.
DECLARE Possession IS ONE OF
    `no licence, class licence or exemption`
    `licensed and within its conditions`
    `licensed but breaching its conditions`
    `exempt from the 2021 Act`

GIVEN `the possession` IS A Possession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession is unlawful possession` IF
    CONSIDER `the possession`
    WHEN `no licence, class licence or exemption` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "use" means "(a) to fire the gun; or (b) to hold the gun so as to cause a reasonable belief that it will be fired,
-- whether or not it is capable of being fired."
GIVEN `fired it` IS A BOOLEAN, `held it so as to cause a reasonable belief it will be fired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gun is used` IF
    `fired it` OR `held it so as to cause a reasonable belief it will be fired`

-- "trafficking in guns" means "to import, supply or transfer 2 or more guns (whether or not of the same kind) in
-- contravention of" the 2021 Act "or any Act, repealed by that Act intending to -- (a) injure, or endanger the safety
-- of, another person; (b) cause reasonable fear of the infliction of injury to another person; or (c) destroy or damage
-- any property". One gun is never trafficking, and trafficking requires one of the listed intentions.
DECLARE Intent IS ONE OF
    `to injure or endanger another person`
    `to cause reasonable fear of injury`
    `to destroy or damage property`
    `to help another person do any of those things with the gun`
    `no harmful intent`

GIVEN `number of guns` IS A NUMBER, `in contravention of the 2021 Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the intent` IS AN Intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is trafficking in guns` IF
        `number of guns` >= 2
    AND `in contravention of the 2021 Act`
    AND CONSIDER `the intent`
        WHEN `to injure or endanger another person` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to cause reasonable fear of injury` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to destroy or damage property` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Schedule -- scheduled offences`

-- The Schedule: (1) unlawful assembly, Penal Code ss 143 to 145; (2) rioting, ss 147, 148 and 152; (3) offences against the
-- person, ss 302, 304, 307, 324 to 327, 329 to 333, 356, 357 and 506; (4) abduction or kidnapping, ss 361, 363 to 367, and
-- Kidnapping Act 1961 ss 3 to 5; (5) extortion, ss 384 to 389; (6) house-breaking, ss 442, 448 to 453, 458A, 459 and 460;
-- (7) robbery, ss 392 to 397, 399 and 402; (8) preventing or resisting arrest, ss 224 and 225; (9) vandalism, Vandalism Act
-- 1966 s 3; (10) mischief, ss 435, 436, 438 and 440. Penal Code s 458A is not an integer and is not encoded.
GIVEN `s` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Penal Code section is a scheduled offence` IF
        `lies between` `s` 143 145
    OR  `s` = 147 OR `s` = 148 OR `s` = 152
    OR  `s` = 302 OR `s` = 304 OR `s` = 307
    OR  `lies between` `s` 324 327
    OR  `lies between` `s` 329 333
    OR  `s` = 356 OR `s` = 357 OR `s` = 506
    OR  `s` = 361
    OR  `lies between` `s` 363 367
    OR  `lies between` `s` 384 389
    OR  `s` = 442
    OR  `lies between` `s` 448 453
    OR  `s` = 459 OR `s` = 460
    OR  `lies between` `s` 392 397
    OR  `s` = 399 OR `s` = 402
    OR  `s` = 224 OR `s` = 225
    OR  `s` = 435 OR `s` = 436 OR `s` = 438 OR `s` = 440

§§ `3 -- carrying a gun with criminal intent`

-- s 3(1): an offence if "(a) the person carries a gun intending to" (i) injure or endanger another; (ii) cause reasonable
-- fear of injury; (iii) destroy or damage property; or (iv) facilitate another person to do any of those "using the gun";
-- "and (b) the person is then in unlawful possession of the gun". "carry" includes "to have on or about an individual's
-- person".
GIVEN `carries the gun` IS A BOOLEAN, `the intent` IS AN Intent, `the possession` IS A Possession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying with criminal intent is an offence` IF
        `carries the gun`
    AND (NOT (`the intent` EQUALS `no harmful intent`))
    AND `the possession is unlawful possession` `the possession`

-- s 3(2): imprisonment "not less than 5 years and not more than 10 years" and caning "not less than 6 strokes". (3): where
-- the person "is proved to have been previously convicted of a scheduled offence", not less than 5 and not more than 20
-- years, and not less than 6 strokes. The minimum does not rise; only the maximum doubles.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the s 3 minimum years` IS 5

GIVEN `previously convicted of a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the s 3 maximum years` IS
    IF `previously convicted of a scheduled offence` THEN 20 ELSE 10

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the s 3 minimum strokes` IS 6

§§ `3A -- carrying a gun during a scheduled offence`

-- s 3A: where a person is convicted of a scheduled offence, the person "shall be punished with imprisonment for life and
-- shall also be punished with caning with not less than 6 strokes" if, "at the time of his committing or at the time of
-- his apprehension for the scheduled offence -- (a) is carrying any gun; and (b) is in unlawful possession of the gun".
-- No intent is required, and carrying at the moment of arrest is enough.
GIVEN `convicted of a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `carrying a gun when committing it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `carrying a gun when apprehended for it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the possession` IS A Possession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `life imprisonment and caning are mandatory under s 3A` IF
        `convicted of a scheduled offence`
    AND (`carrying a gun when committing it` OR `carrying a gun when apprehended for it`)
    AND `the possession is unlawful possession` `the possession`

§§ `4 and 4A -- using a gun`

-- s 4(1): "Subject to any exception mentioned in Chapter 4 of the Penal Code 1871 which may be applicable (other than
-- section 95)", any person who "uses or attempts to use any gun intending to injure, or endanger the safety of, another
-- person, to cause reasonable fear of the infliction of injury or to destroy or damage any property" is guilty and "shall
-- on conviction be punished with death". (2): a person who uses or attempts to use a gun "shall, until the contrary is
-- proved, be presumed" to have had that intent.
DECLARE Exception IS ONE OF
    `no Chapter 4 exception applies`
    `a Chapter 4 exception other than section 95 applies`
    `only the section 95 exception applies`

GIVEN `the exception` IS AN Exception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Chapter 4 exception excuses the use` IF
    `the exception` EQUALS `a Chapter 4 exception other than section 95 applies`

GIVEN `used or attempted to use a gun` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the contrary of a harmful intent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the exception` IS AN Exception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using a gun is a capital offence under s 4` IF
        `used or attempted to use a gun`
    AND (NOT `proved the contrary of a harmful intent`)
    AND (NOT (`a Chapter 4 exception excuses the use` `the exception`))

-- s 4A: subject to the same exceptions, any person who "uses or attempts to use any gun at the time of his or her
-- committing or attempting to commit any scheduled offence shall, whether or not the person has any intention to cause
-- physical injury to any individual or property", be "punished with death". No presumption is needed, and none can be
-- rebutted: intent is irrelevant.
GIVEN `used or attempted to use a gun` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `while committing or attempting a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the exception` IS AN Exception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using a gun in a scheduled offence is a capital offence under s 4A` IF
        `used or attempted to use a gun`
    AND `while committing or attempting a scheduled offence`
    AND (NOT (`a Chapter 4 exception excuses the use` `the exception`))

§§ `5 -- accomplices`

-- s 5: "Where any gun is used by any person in committing or in attempting to commit ANY offence or where an offence under
-- section 4A has been committed", each accomplice "present at the scene of the offence who may reasonably be presumed to
-- have known that the person was carrying or had in the person's possession or under the person's control the gun",
-- shall, "unless the accomplice proves that he or she had taken all reasonable steps to prevent the use of the gun", be
-- "punished with death". "Any offence" is not limited to scheduled offences.
GIVEN `a gun was used in committing or attempting any offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an s 4A offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accomplice was present at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accomplice may reasonably be presumed to have known of the gun` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accomplice proved all reasonable steps to prevent its use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accomplice is guilty of a capital offence under s 5` IF
        (`a gun was used in committing or attempting any offence` OR `an s 4A offence was committed`)
    AND `the accomplice was present at the scene`
    AND `the accomplice may reasonably be presumed to have known of the gun`
    AND (NOT `the accomplice proved all reasonable steps to prevent its use`)

§§ `6 -- trafficking`

-- s 6(1): trafficking in guns is punished with "(a) death; or (b) imprisonment for life and with caning with not less than
-- 6 strokes". s 6(2) is deleted.
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `life imprisonment and at least 6 strokes`
    `life imprisonment alone`
    `20 years' imprisonment and 6 strokes`

GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punishment is open to the court under s 6` IF
    CONSIDER `the punishment`
    WHEN `death` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `life imprisonment and at least 6 strokes` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- consorting`

-- s 7: a person who "consorts with, or is found in the company of, another person who is unlawfully carrying or is in
-- unlawful possession of any gun in circumstances which raise a reasonable presumption that he or she knew" of the gun is
-- guilty, "unless he or she proves that he or she had reasonable grounds for believing that that other person was not
-- unlawfully carrying or was not in unlawful possession of the gun", and is liable "to the like punishment as that other
-- person". The punishment is borrowed, not fixed.
GIVEN `consorted with or was in the company of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the other person's possession` IS A Possession,
      `circumstances raise a reasonable presumption of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved reasonable grounds to believe the possession was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consorting is an offence under s 7` IF
        `consorted with or was in the company of the other person`
    AND `the possession is unlawful possession` `the other person's possession`
    AND `circumstances raise a reasonable presumption of knowledge`
    AND (NOT `proved reasonable grounds to believe the possession was lawful`)

§§ `8 -- imitation guns`

-- s 8: any person who "at the time of committing or attempting to commit or abetting the commission of any scheduled
-- offence exhibits any imitation gun in a manner likely to put any other person in fear of death or hurt" is liable "to
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years and shall also be punished with caning with not less than 3
-- strokes". A real gun is not an imitation gun, so s 8 does not reach it.
GIVEN `the object` IS AN Object,
      `while committing, attempting or abetting a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exhibited in a manner likely to put a person in fear of death or hurt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exhibiting an imitation gun is an offence under s 8` IF
        `the object is an imitation gun` `the object`
    AND `while committing, attempting or abetting a scheduled offence`
    AND `exhibited in a manner likely to put a person in fear of death or hurt`

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the s 8 maximum years` IS 10

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the s 8 minimum strokes` IS 3

§§ `9 -- the occupier's presumption`

-- s 9: where a gun is found in or on any premises, "the occupier of the premises is deemed to be in possession of the gun
-- unless the occupier proves that some other person was in possession thereof, or the occupier had no knowledge or
-- reasonable means of knowing that the gun was in or on the premises and that the occupier had taken all reasonable
-- precautions against the gun being kept in or on the premises". The second escape needs BOTH ignorance AND precautions.
GIVEN `a gun was found on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier proved another person possessed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier proved no knowledge or reasonable means of knowing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier proved all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is deemed to possess the gun` IF
        `a gun was found on the premises`
    AND (NOT `the occupier proved another person possessed it`)
    AND (NOT (`the occupier proved no knowledge or reasonable means of knowing` AND `the occupier proved all reasonable precautions`))
